{"cases":[{"case_id":"feature-010442eca646a6c824e8","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["example"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["positive_example"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","negated_alternative","positive_example"],"text":"For the Atlas project, please keep the screen-reader labels modeled on the concise labels from the last settings panel; that example worked well, instead of expanding them into extra descriptions."},{"case_id":"feature-0386a0d2b98e29e6cdaa","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["prompt_rule"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["prompt_rule"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["direct","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","prompt_rule"],"text":"Keep module boundaries explicit and do not let modules reach into each other's private internals."},{"case_id":"feature-0431b276bdbe5660899c","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["memory"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","memory","negated_alternative"],"text":"The Orion project runs its command examples on Ubuntu with zsh installed."},{"case_id":"feature-06a7b0971ef459070cf5","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["procedure"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["procedure"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","procedure","typos"],"text":"When the Nova project changes its supported language version, check the compiler matrix first, then update the version notes and examples."},{"case_id":"feature-077b4f0cbeb2d639d602","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["procedure"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["correction"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["correction","feature_holdout","fragment","permanent_profile"],"text":"The earlier time-zone handling was off. Convert times to the user's zone first, then show the original zone beside them."},{"case_id":"feature-0dfafe26d9e2017eeb88","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["example"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["positive_example"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["emphatic","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","positive_example"],"text":"The runtime-version summary you gave last time is exactly the model to follow going forward—short, clear, and grouped by support status."},{"case_id":"feature-0f16dbcc5eb7ebf9b6d9","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["example"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["correction"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["contrastive","correction","feature_holdout","permanent_profile"],"text":"The old trace fields were too vague; use a concrete example such as request_id, actor, and elapsed_ms so each field's purpose is obvious."},{"case_id":"feature-13d7bfa3474a00623aae","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["preference"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["preference"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","indirect","preference"],"text":"For the Cedar project, I’d lean toward shorter fixture names in future."},{"case_id":"feature-1655539a1af93bced055","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["procedure"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["correction"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["correction","current_context","feature_holdout","negated_alternative"],"text":"For the Vega project, don't run validation after packaging; validate the source first, then package only the passing result."},{"case_id":"feature-195d453b27f91df5b7da","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["memory"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["conversational","current_context","feature_holdout","memory"],"text":"The Harbor project keeps its archived reports under a separate yearly folder."},{"case_id":"feature-1cbcc96d6ff7965e3fe8","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["memory"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["contrastive","feature_holdout","memory","permanent_profile"],"text":"I work across calendar systems where the week can begin on different days."},{"case_id":"feature-1e0c82dd4e91abc96617","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["memory"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","memory","typos"],"text":"The Lumen project build logs are saved on a shared CI volume, not my laptop."},{"case_id":"feature-1f8177b650ae3c4079ef","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["memory"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","indirect","memory"],"text":"In the Pine project, I usually read change summaries from my phone during handoffs."},{"case_id":"feature-223e39c8dbce1186b01f","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["preference"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["preference"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["conversational","current_context","feature_holdout","preference"],"text":"For the Iris project, I’d prefer the design tokens to stay close to the existing naming style."},{"case_id":"feature-25d7648b31c7ccc2f91d","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["procedure"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["procedure"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["direct","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","procedure"],"text":"When preparing an invoice, confirm the recipient's required format first, then render the invoice in that format."},{"case_id":"feature-2e6a6fde21e1e165c557","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["preference"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["preference"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["feature_holdout","fragment","permanent_profile","preference"],"text":"Diagnostic notes: a little more concise, please."},{"case_id":"feature-2f4d423e51866824589d","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["prompt_rule"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["prompt_rule"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["conversational","current_context","feature_holdout","prompt_rule"],"text":"In the Sol project, network fallbacks must fail visibly rather than silently returning stale data."},{"case_id":"feature-3124edd2486658c611ed","expectation":{"accepted_routes":[],"accepted_signal_kinds":["revocation"],"affected_artifact_id":"artifact-35dfe08ae9276274","durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","negated_alternative","revocation"],"text":"For the Nimbus project, remove artifact-35dfe08ae9276274 from the active sync-backup adaptation; I don't want that behavior applied anymore."},{"case_id":"feature-33a9162360ceb64fd133","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["preference"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["correction"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["conversational","correction","current_context","feature_holdout"],"text":"The earlier test commands were too noisy for the Kestrel project; I’d rather see the focused command for the changed area."},{"case_id":"feature-33d55b706041a2b31b39","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["preference"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["correction"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["correction","emphatic","feature_holdout","permanent_profile"],"text":"Please stop making my user prompts overly formal—use a warmer, more conversational style from now on!"},{"case_id":"feature-41e80da8e7d0a1f868ea","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["example"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["positive_example"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","indirect","positive_example"],"text":"The rollback checklist from the last Falcon release is a good pattern to reuse later."},{"case_id":"feature-43c2d78a1d27d79fa6a7","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["prompt_rule"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["prompt_rule"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","prompt_rule","typos"],"text":"In the Birch project, package updates shouldnt change unrelated lockfile entries."},{"case_id":"feature-48deb873fe55ee0adb9d","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["prompt_rule"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["prompt_rule"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","negated_alternative","prompt_rule"],"text":"For the Echo project, privacy labels must not expose personal identifiers."},{"case_id":"feature-48f205cd684bc5a795a5","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["procedure"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["procedure"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["ambiguous","conversational","current_context","feature_holdout"],"text":"In the Juniper project, keep the workspace root fixed to the repository, and whenever it changes, verify the configured tools resolve from that root before continuing."},{"case_id":"feature-539af56e94fa02b1e339","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["prompt_rule"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["prompt_rule"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["feature_holdout","fragment","permanent_profile","prompt_rule"],"text":"Notification timing: do not send reminders during my local quiet hours."},{"case_id":"feature-5440080699a98d36dc28","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["prompt_rule"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["prompt_rule"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["emphatic","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","prompt_rule"],"text":"Preview commands must be read-only—no exceptions."},{"case_id":"feature-5bccf87a46df435a43d9","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["memory"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["feature_holdout","fragment","memory","permanent_profile"],"text":"I tend to work with branch names that include ticket numbers."},{"case_id":"feature-6120e7f80ba5d4b2d475","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["procedure"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["procedure"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["conversational","current_context","feature_holdout","procedure"],"text":"When an issue is ready for review in the Quartz project, apply the review label first, then add it to the review queue."},{"case_id":"feature-6d8cef387938cfa6238b","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["preference"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["preference"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["emphatic","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","preference"],"text":"Handoff notes should feel more practical and less polished."},{"case_id":"feature-7406c5429d1f22f755c6","expectation":{"accepted_routes":[],"accepted_signal_kinds":["revocation"],"affected_artifact_id":"artifact-a3547d599a6d6738","durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["conversational","current_context","feature_holdout","revocation"],"text":"Please remove artifact-a3547d599a6d6738 from the active secret-scan adaptation in the Maple project."},{"case_id":"feature-776db522092d6ebc28e9","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["prompt_rule"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["prompt_rule"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","indirect","prompt_rule"],"text":"In the Sable project, permission reviews must include the effective access level."},{"case_id":"feature-77768b73331156b2675c","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["preference"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["preference"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","negated_alternative","preference"],"text":"For the Drift project, I’d rather assign one clear incident owner than split ownership across several people."},{"case_id":"feature-77f0aad880546cacc50e","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["example"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["positive_example"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["contrastive","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","positive_example"],"text":"The review queue format from your previous response is the one to imitate; the compact owner-and-status rows were useful."},{"case_id":"feature-7a291df1ccc7884087f3","expectation":{"accepted_routes":[],"accepted_signal_kinds":["revocation"],"affected_artifact_id":"artifact-422220f8aa4338f0","durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["emphatic","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","revocation"],"text":"Remove artifact-422220f8aa4338f0 from the active support-rotation adaptation now."},{"case_id":"feature-7afd74e56411806df535","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["example"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["positive_example"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","positive_example","typos"],"text":"The research-claim wording in the last Rowan project summary was good, keep using that pattern."},{"case_id":"feature-7ec388682e39375b2db6","expectation":{"accepted_routes":[],"accepted_signal_kinds":["revocation"],"affected_artifact_id":"artifact-f4f3bb9ea7712bfd","durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["feature_holdout","fragment","permanent_profile","revocation"],"text":"Shell dialects: remove artifact-f4f3bb9ea7712bfd from my active adaptation."},{"case_id":"feature-84f83fbd0e6b5f7501c1","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["memory"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["ambiguous","contrastive","feature_holdout","permanent_profile"],"text":"I work with dependency updates mostly in npm projects, and I prefer seeing the smallest compatible upgrade rather than a broad refresh."},{"case_id":"feature-87e867f46186d88198ba","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["example"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["positive_example"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["conversational","current_context","feature_holdout","positive_example"],"text":"The release notes you wrote for the Vale project last time are a great example to follow."},{"case_id":"feature-8d2cd36173ecae9e0ce8","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["memory"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["ambiguous","current_context","feature_holdout","negated_alternative"],"text":"In the Ember project, the review checklist already covers the steps I use; when the checklist is updated, run through those checks before opening the review."},{"case_id":"feature-8e8f5f9dd850fb5aee03","expectation":{"accepted_routes":[],"accepted_signal_kinds":["revocation"],"affected_artifact_id":"artifact-1d0e28782511a9a9","durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","revocation","typos"],"text":"In the Rook project, remove artifact-1d0e28782511a9a9 from the active source-citation adaptation, please."},{"case_id":"feature-92143d8ad0b8cf0fb0ed","expectation":{"accepted_routes":[],"accepted_signal_kinds":["revocation"],"affected_artifact_id":"artifact-b7e54d25e21272b6","durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","indirect","revocation"],"text":"For the Slate project, please remove artifact-b7e54d25e21272b6 from the active storage-limit adaptation."},{"case_id":"feature-95d204460a26c452c0df","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["example"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["positive_example"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["feature_holdout","fragment","permanent_profile","positive_example"],"text":"That earlier scoped-request example is the pattern I want followed."},{"case_id":"feature-9b2b68caa2e515de120b","expectation":{"accepted_routes":[],"accepted_signal_kinds":["revocation"],"affected_artifact_id":"artifact-698f373c85d82b58","durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["contrastive","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","revocation"],"text":"I no longer want artifact-698f373c85d82b58 shaping my status updates; remove it from the active adaptation."},{"case_id":"feature-9d65e4baa5a861bc7de0","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["prompt_rule"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["prompt_rule"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["contrastive","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","prompt_rule"],"text":"Paths containing spaces must be quoted before they are passed to commands."},{"case_id":"feature-a2334fa983fa22820433","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["procedure"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["procedure"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","negated_alternative","procedure"],"text":"When the Aspen project changes its migration files, inspect the migration plan first, then run the checks against a fresh database."},{"case_id":"feature-a59d5f4035fa01b56259","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["preference"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["preference"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["contrastive","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","preference"],"text":"Error reports could be a bit more concise in future."},{"case_id":"feature-a6f02b523a207014c401","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["memory"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["ambiguous","direct","feature_holdout","permanent_profile"],"text":"I usually work with pinned versions, and I prefer keeping those pins visible rather than resolving them away."},{"case_id":"feature-a7143e5a67fcc90f0447","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["memory"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["ambiguous","current_context","feature_holdout","typos"],"text":"For the Briar project, approval records are kept in the release folder; when one is added, check the approver and timestamp before marking the change complete."},{"case_id":"feature-a7baea0e70e47f765b95","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["memory"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["emphatic","feature_holdout","memory","permanent_profile"],"text":"My clients are spread across North American and European regions."},{"case_id":"feature-aa5fb8d59d7750eed0b5","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["preference"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["preference"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["direct","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","preference"],"text":"Deployment windows should ideally stay in the quieter evening hours."},{"case_id":"feature-aca4538b12a35e7a8c63","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["procedure"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["procedure"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["emphatic","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","procedure"],"text":"When a meeting ends, capture the meeting record first, then send the summary to the attendees."},{"case_id":"feature-b26d7e950f9c5ba3bc6f","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["procedure"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["procedure"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["contrastive","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","procedure"],"text":"When a local cache gets stale, clear it first and then rebuild it from the current source."},{"case_id":"feature-bea19a853d3c3698f09b","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["correction"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["correction","direct","feature_holdout","permanent_profile"],"text":"The earlier task-owner note was wrong; I’m the person who handles these tasks, not the team lead."},{"case_id":"feature-cd93c5bbd34051644dd3","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["procedure"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["procedure"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["ambiguous","current_context","feature_holdout","indirect"],"text":"In the Cinder project, failure messages should identify the failed operation and must not reveal secrets; after an error, capture the operation name before presenting the message."},{"case_id":"feature-d23a09b9a6a821bda0c0","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["procedure"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["procedure"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["feature_holdout","fragment","permanent_profile","procedure"],"text":"When keyboard navigation changes, test the tab order first, then check the focus styling."},{"case_id":"feature-d6384d91d907c08d4f37","expectation":{"accepted_routes":[],"accepted_signal_kinds":["revocation"],"affected_artifact_id":"artifact-f42760856521a1b1","durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["direct","feature_holdout","permanent_profile","revocation"],"text":"Remove artifact-f42760856521a1b1 from the active search-filter adaptation."},{"case_id":"feature-ddb072f3482b368a3902","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["example"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["positive_example"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["ambiguous","emphatic","feature_holdout","permanent_profile"],"text":"Use output examples like the short before-and-after table you gave previously, and keep examples clearly separated from the actual answer."},{"case_id":"feature-e29e02318159c35a4353","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["preference"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["preference"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","preference","typos"],"text":"For the Elm project, I’d probably keep document headings fairly compact."},{"case_id":"feature-e510442e8c57bda6b185","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["example"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["positive_example"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["ambiguous","feature_holdout","fragment","permanent_profile"],"text":"Writing tone should follow the friendly example from before, while staying professional and avoiding exaggerated claims."},{"case_id":"feature-ebdb08420bab9151b10e","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["procedure"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["procedure"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["current_context","feature_holdout","indirect","procedure"],"text":"When logs reach the retention threshold in the Firth project, archive them first, then delete only the expired copies."},{"case_id":"feature-f2e7b2b614eef2b2c449","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["correction"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"current_context"},"split":"holdout","tags":["correction","current_context","feature_holdout","indirect"],"text":"The earlier usage-budget note was outdated; my current plan has a lower monthly limit."},{"case_id":"feature-f409af4e4592bd7e8212","expectation":{"accepted_routes":["memory"],"accepted_signal_kinds":["memory"],"durable_signal":true,"scope_hint":"permanent_profile"},"split":"holdout","tags":["direct","feature_holdout","memory